    {
      "id": "a58f4b0fc39a97ea5b34db40df77366efc0dcd91",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": true,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 506465366,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> By protocol analyzers.\n\nI know of one protocol analyzer where, if it ever displays sizes as hex rather than decimal, that's a bug that needs to be fixed; it has a name like \"Wire something-or-other\". :-)\n\nAre there *other* protocol analyzers that show sizes in hex?  Do they think their users grew up in a culture where everybody has 16 fingers?",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-02-10T21:02:34.350Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-02-10T21:37:43.068Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 88035840,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2021-02-10T23:23:54.072Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2045,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 506480482,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The topic is not worth the bytes we spend in these comments.\n\nYou have it your way, I print the size in hex and in decimal.\n\nAgain, the reason is that Wiireshark (despite what you just said) consistently prints size in HEX for storage protocols that use RDMA or network (see NVME or ISCSI). I have not written it,  it is done by someone else and it would be consistent with any commercial analyzer I have tried. And I want two packets aside each other to show the same numbers. It would be difficult to convert HEX to decimal and vice versa in the head. Two packets that follow each other must show the same encoding.\n\nI am not here to start a flame war over nothing. But to help. There are other changes in the queue that are much more material than this cosmetic thing.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8151300,
            "username": "constg2021",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Constantine Gavrilov",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3e14dae3452c6729ef51dfff170770b32fcab39df75873fde50fce93c6d61b49?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/constg2021"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-02-10T21:37:43.031Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-02-10T21:38:32.126Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 88035840,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
