        {
          "id": 506500747,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> Again, the reason is that Wiireshark (despite what you just said) consistently prints size in HEX for storage protocols that use RDMA or network (see NVME or ISCSI).\n\nWhat I said was\n\n> I know of one protocol analyzer where, if it ever displays sizes as hex rather than decimal, that's a bug that needs to be fixed; it has a name like \"Wire something-or-other\". :-)\n\nI.e., if Wireshark does that, *it's a bug that needs to be fixed*.  I will fix those.",
