        {
          "id": 506546685,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Rebase it first, which means the size will be printed as DEC_HEX (as sequence numbers, counts, lengths/sizes, etc. should be if they're not just printed in decimal), as a result of 9e2e260fa8f0c7ca4685542c92053ac7ecf3f4a0, which also changes the hex stuff in the iSCSI and NVME dissectors to be DEC_HEX.\n\nThen the only changes left will be to the address and key.",
